  "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4 & =c{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(3-c){y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=4,$ which is an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2,$ which is a circle.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true.",
